        { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is the difference between hourglass and pear body shape?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "An hourglass shape has a bust and hips that are nearly equal with a dramatically smaller waist in between. A pear shape has hips noticeably wider than the bust, with a waist that is present but not as sharply defined." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is high hip measurement and why does it matter?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The high hip is measured approximately 3 to 4 inches (8–10 cm) below the natural waist, around the upper hip area. It feeds the High Hip-to-Waist ratio shown in your result, which can flag a pronounced shelf pattern at the top of the hip that bust/waist/hip alone can miss." } },
